A||||3||Areakon||Building a 3.4||||1||
Z||000000||Areakon||09-22-2001||02:22 AM||||This winter I'm planning on putting a 3.4 pushrod in place of the 2.8 in my car. I've decided on the 3.4 for ease of installation and keeping the original look. So what exactly can be done to the 3.4 to get more Hp and Torque. I've heard of putting some of the 3.4 DOHC internals in to up the compression. Is there any truth to this? Are the pistons domed or are the connection rods a different length in the DOHC? I'm also wondering if the 2.8 heads will fit the 3.4 or am I going to have to invest in a set of 3.4 heads?||||reg||1
Z||000001||tgowens||09-22-2001||03:52 AM||||everything from the heads up on a 2.8 will bolt onto a 3.4.........there are several threads about upping the HP -- just do a "search" on here for 3.4 and you will find all sorts of info including the bracket and starter mods to do to the 3.4 block.....||||reg||1
Z||000002||Areakon||09-22-2001||04:42 AM||||I've looked through the archives and I have yet to find a listing of internal mods done to the 3.4 pushrod motor. I found lots of topics pretraining to the starter holes and welding the bolt in place. But none talking directly about putting in some of the internals of the 3.4 TDC motor. Which I have seen a few references to in other 3.4 topics.||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||09-22-2001||11:02 AM||||The only difference between the 3.4 pushrod engine and the 3.4 DOHC engine as far as reciprocating assembly is concerned are the pistons. The crankshaft and rods are the same. <P>You can use the 3.4 DOHC pistons in your 3.4-liter pushrod motor to give you an approximate compression ratio of around 9.7-1 with the iron heads. I almost did this but chose not to because the valve pockets in the piston head are places where detonation can start. They have too many sharp edges too. The stock pistons give you a 9.0-1 compression ratio and have a nice dish in them. The flame front will travel better across a dish piston making them more efficient and more resistant to knock. You can get the stock pistons in hypereutectic from Federal Mogul. <P>The fiero 2.8 iron heads and the Camaro 3.4 iron heads are exactly the same, just the valve springs are different. You could use either one and it would not matter.<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/008285.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/008285.html</A>   <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/calgaryfieros/3400engine.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/calgaryfieros/3400engine.htm</A>   <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html</A>  <A HREF="http://lrp.zon.se/fiero/links.html" TARGET=_blank>http://lrp.zon.se/fiero/links.html</A>  <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/on/freddysplace/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/on/freddysplace/</A>  <A HREF="http://www.s-series.org/htm/windstorm/project-windstorm-stage3.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.s-series.org/htm/windstorm/project-windstorm-stage3.htm</A> <P><BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
